-- title:
--   Isogeny bridge to the special formal mathcal O_D-module
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$, a commutative ring $\mathcal O$ and an element $\pi\in\mathcal O$ with $(r)=(\pi)$, together with an $\mathcal O$-algebra $Onr$ such that the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ is maximal and every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree has a root modulo that ideal; write $k_0 := Onr/(\pi)$. Let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ and $\mathrm{coord}:\Lambda\to \mathbb Z_{r^2}^{\,2}$ (with $\mathbb Z_{r^2}$ the Witt vectors of $\mathbb F_{r^2}$) a map satisfying `IsOrderCoord`: it is additive and injective, sends $1$ to $(1,0)$, is multiplicative for the twisted rule $(x_1,x_2)(y_1,y_2)=(x_1y_1+r\,x_2\varphi(y_2),\,x_1y_2+x_2\varphi(y_1))$ with $\varphi$ the Frobenius, has dense image modulo every power of $r$, and satisfies $\mathrm{coord}(m)_1+\varphi(\mathrm{coord}(m)_1)=n$ whenever $m+\bar m=n$. Let $A_0$ be a `FakeEllipticCurve` of level $N$ over $k_0$ (a smooth proper abelian scheme with commutative relative group law, connected two-dimensional fibres, and a $\Lambda$-action compatible with the group law and with traces), let $X_0$ be a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $k_0$ (a commutative two-dimensional formal group with a $\mathbb Z_{r^2}$-action and a uniformiser series $\varpi$ with $\varpi\circ\varpi=[r]$ and $\varpi\circ[a]=[\varphi a]\circ\varpi$) whose multiplication by $r$ has kernel of degree $r^4$, and let $\theta_0$ be a system of two-dimensional formal coordinates for $A_0.f$ such that `IsFormalModuleVia` holds: $\theta_0$ are formal coordinates for the group law of $A_0$ with formal group $X_0.F$, and the action of each $m\in\Lambda$ on nilpotent points corresponds to the series $[\mathrm{coord}(m)_1]+[\mathrm{coord}(m)_2]\circ\varpi$. Let further $\iota:\mathbb Z_{r^2}\to Onr$ be a ring homomorphism and $\Phi$ a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $Onr/(r)$ which is special for the reduction of $\iota$ (its Lie algebra is the direct sum of the two eigen-submodules $\mathrm{lieZero}$ and $\mathrm{lieOne}$, both invertible) and whose multiplication by $r$ has kernel of degree $r^4$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a ring homomorphism $\kappa:k_0\to Onr/(r)$ compatible with the two quotient maps from $Onr$, a natural number $n_0$, and a pair of power series $\beta_0$ in two variables over $Onr/(r)$ which is an $\mathcal O_D$-homomorphism $\Phi\to \kappa_*X_0$ whose kernel has degree $r^{4n_0}$.
--
--   This is the link, in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation, between the formal $\mathcal O_D$-module of a fake elliptic curve at a supersingular point of the special fibre and Drinfeld's special formal $\mathcal O_D$-module: any two such objects of height $4$ over the residue field are joined by an isogeny of height divisible by $4$. It feeds the construction of the fine-level Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation with Atkin–Lehner data.
